From be32bf4baf49fcdfd45336ac8707546fc528625c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:09:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: one card per incident when a board's
 replica stays behind the feed head or its loop stalls

Card t_01a1d3df5e5d0757. 2026-11-12: three stale replicas raised no alarm.
- hermes-hub: the default loop slowed from a round a minute to one every 15-28 min from ~17:27 PT; the
  replica's pulled_at stayed at 02:06:53 UTC past 02:39 and hub cards did not promote (t_01a1d2cc49634a78).
- laptop-1: ~75k changes behind for hours after a sleep, until ~22:30 PT (t_01a1d36ddcea59fe), found only
  through false parent_missing blocks and wrong "ready with no worker" notices.
- laptop-1 23:53:44 PT: `kanban sync: default not synced: this core does not declare columns ...`
  (SchemaAhead), then no more rounds; four cards waiting on done remote parents froze.

Why: nothing watched replica freshness itself. pulled_at had only consumers, and since #1931 those consumers
wait silently on a stale replica (a DEBUG/INFO trace). #1934's outbox alarm skips a failing loop "which other
alarms cover", and no such alarm existed. Root: no component owned replica freshness; the gate tests assert the
gate defers, none that a long deferral surfaces.

Fix: hermes_cli/kanban_sync_replica_age.py, run by kanban_sync_outbox_age.check on the dispatcher tick (outside
the sync loop, so a dead, stuck or given-up loop is seen too).
- Per board in mode primary/shadow: (replica pulled_at, monotonic time first seen). A missing or unreadable
  replica is a stamp that has not advanced. No advance for REPLICA_STALE_S = 1200 s of monotonic time (2x
  FRESH_SECONDS) opens an incident: ONE card through the outbox card's report path (comment at most hourly on
  an open card, a new card once it is done). Monotonic time stands still while a Mac sleeps.
- The stamp advancing ends the incident (one INFO line). One INFO telemetry line per board per hour.
- The card names host + gateway, board, the replica stamp in PT, awake minutes, the last round's outcome
  (behind / failed: <error> / no sync round since T), the loop's recorded stop (.sync-state.json: a give-up
  names its refusal), pending outbox ops, the running core sha, and every local card waiting on a remote
  parent with that parent's Board status (row_evidence, 15 s budget; the local mirror when unreachable), with
  the stuck-card-recovery.md item 3 brief (precedent t_01a1d42acdce8e23).
- after_round feeds each round's outcome to the check; report() takes key/author/title/body; the outbox
  check's comment now cites this check instead of "no alarm covers a failing loop yet".
- Detached/unsynced boards never file; an exception inside the check is logged and never reaches the tick.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_replica_age.py, fake mono + wall clocks), RED on a stub (13 failed,
4 never-file passed), GREEN 17/17: rounds behind 21 min, URLError rounds, dead loop, no/unreadable replica,
5 h wall jump in 1 awake min, close + comment + new card after done, detached, unsynced, exception, tick
wiring, card contents, frozen children (Board done / mirror fallback), and replays: hub slow rounds fires
18:27 PT; MacBook 75k backlog after a 10 h sleep fires 18:20 PT (20 awake min after 08:00), one card through
22:30; MacBook SchemaAhead give-up fires 00:13 PT naming the refusal and core sha. Sync suites: 58 files,
1357 passed.
